    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the NSDataAsset class
      </heading>
      <class name="NSDataAsset" super="NSObject" ovadd="10.11.0">
        <declared>AppKit/NSDataAsset.h</declared>
        <conform>NSCopying</conform>
        <desc>
          NSDataAsset provides a convenient interface for
          accessing data resources stored within application
          bundles. This class enables loading and managing
          data assets that are packaged with applications, such as
          configuration files, templates, reference data,
          or any binary content that needs to be accessible at
          runtime. Data assets are identified by name and can
          be loaded from the main bundle or from specified bundles.
          The class automatically handles resource location,
          loading, and type identification based on file
          extensions and bundle organization. NSDataAsset
          simplifies resource management by providing a
          unified interface for accessing bundled data
          regardless of the underlying file system structure
          or bundle configuration.
        </desc>
